<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>🔴 Macron orders plan to protect France critical infrastructure against 'Russian hybrid attacks'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a606176c873499da9f6d99ce27395d9bb3e712eb46874972cd08916af4049fe8</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:24:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260918-macron-orders-plan-to-protect-france-critical-infrastructure-against-russian-hybrid-attacks" /></entry><entry><title>Macron orders plan to protect France's critical infrastructure against 'Russian hybrid attacks'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e7450d5fd0c986d5a513e7095995bda836091573c95327514d408d588a3ebd4</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T12:23:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260918-macron-orders-plan-to-protect-france-critical-infrastructure-against-russian-hybrid-attacks" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron on Friday said he had ordered measures to protect France's critical infrastructure and defence industry sites from "Russian hybrid attacks", adding that the threat from Moscow had intensified in recent weeks.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Prized Aztec codex returns to Mexico on loan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09cbd840e01b22be5eb3de483bd44cf8e3a30e5973666d9abd079ba0b15165c0</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:44:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-prized-aztec-codex-returns-to-mexico-on-loan" /><summary type="html">A cherished 16th-century Mexican manuscript that tells the history of the Aztecs in pictograms went on display Thursday in Mexico City, nearly two centuries after it was whisked off to France. France's National Library, which has maintained possession of it for over a century, loaned it to Mexico to commemorate 200 years of relations between the two countries, although Mexico is pushing for its permanent return.</summary></entry><entry><title>France’s Yellow Vests to return as fuel prices soar?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f917023fc3d5e587a994309398f90cd25b740474299afaa7a34323c99dd52b66</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:43:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-france-s-yellow-vests-to-return-as-fuel-prices-soar" /><summary type="html">Eight years after fuel taxes helped spark the Yellow Vest movement, calls for a return to the streets are gathering momentum in France amid soaring energy prices. Recent days have seen fishermen blockading ports and oil terminals in protest at price hikes, but they are far from the only group feeling the squeeze.</summary></entry><entry><title>How will rise of AI impact Africa?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f9b4c63d014a55797c9cca7eabf439a6c4702a74905708e32372dbd3984f8c1</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:06:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-how-will-rise-of-ai-impact-africa" /><summary type="html">The threat of catastrophic danger as artificial intelligence develops at high speed has sparked a global debate on how it should be regulated. And Africa is no exception. As governments and businesses look to harness the technology, concerns are growing over jobs, misinformation and the need for safeguards.</summary></entry><entry><title>The Cameroon civil society groups taking on gender-based violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ff2629ef5ec4a408ed9fbc8848687e20dd9cc1552dafd283d8cf9bd898a6c5e</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T10:54:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-the-cameroon-civil-society-groups-taking-on-gender-based-violence" /><summary type="html">August 2026 has been a particularly tragic month for women in Cameroon, as eight cases of femicides were recorded in eight days. These figures add to the sixty or so cases already recorded since the start of the year by the Ministry of Women's Empowerment and the Family. On the ground, associations are mobilising to provide legal and psychological support to families in a country where a complaint of domestic violence rarely leads to a conviction. Indira Ayuk, Richard and Giresse Ngaana report from Yaoundé.</summary></entry><entry><title>France’s Macron summons party leaders for talks on Mideast and Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c08b4bf08b1cff50aa38e8c043bf9fe0369d391f1da2e8938376424f783e692c</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T10:24:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-france-s-macron-summons-party-leaders-for-talks-on-mideast-and-ukraine" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron is meeting leaders of France’s political parties at the Elysée on Friday for talks on the wars in the Middle East and Ukraine and the consequences for the country’s security and energy amid soaring fuel prices.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russian elections a ‘veneer of democracy’ with opposition barred from running</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4da810e514545ee4dcba9e8f765a3fe7b82f021a4c5aceb5ccedc0d320410dd5</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T10:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/russian-elections-a-veneer-of-democracy-with-opposition-barred-from-running" /><summary type="html">PRESS REVIEW – Friday, September 18: Russia holds its first parliamentary elections since the Ukraine war. Since only parties loyal to Vladimir Putin are running, the elections are seen as nothing but a veneer of democracy. In sports: Zinedine Zidane will unveil his first selection as coach of the French football team. Brisbane 2032 Olympic and Paralympic organisers approve a croc-infested river to hold canoe and rowing events. Finally, the first new feline species in a century has been discovered.</summary><category term="Press Review" /></entry><entry><title>Venezuela lifts block on some news sites as transition talks resume</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc6f2d944cd90ff131a454299a9e6a040bf1a89e57b2db82542b98546fddbf61</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T10:04:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-venezuela-lifts-block-on-some-news-sites-as-transition-talks-resume" /><summary type="html">Venezuela has unblocked some news sites that had been censored for years, its telecom regulator said Thursday, as US-backed political transition talks were set to resume. Digital rights group VE Sin Filtro verified access to 17 news sites through several internet providers. However, at least 188 websites remain blocked, it said, including 79 news outlets.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia votes in wartime election set to secure the Kremlin's power</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be7d33a7c3ec2698d44b13bfb53b40a42f8db002199a47eaa3a53196248f7264</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T09:52:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-russia-votes-in-wartime-election-set-to-secure-the-kremlin-s-power" /><summary type="html">Voting got ⁠underway on Friday in a tightly controlled three-day parliamentary election in Russia which President Vladimir Putin has framed as a barometer of support for Russia's war in Ukraine. It is the first parliamentary election since Russia launched its full-scale war in Ukraine in February 2022, and most anti-war candidates have been excluded from the ballot.</summary></entry><entry><title>Police move hundreds of migrants still in Ceuta off beaches in Spanish enclave</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63a23179a97cc59146341b03197fa5349fc8214085870a5d86d7c70ae958e324</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T09:51:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-police-move-hundreds-of-migrants-still-in-ceuta-off-beaches-in-spanish-enclave" /><summary type="html">Spanish police in Ceuta on Friday morning started moving hundreds of migrants from the beaches of the Spanish enclave to a new tented area. Several thousand migrants remain in Ceuta after tens of thousands of people crossed the border with Morocco in late July.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>UN mission says grounds to believe US committed war crimes in Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b209be2fd6ee48e86339ed3c635a9daa2899e159bd5ca5b3261ac227221e12e</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T09:31:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-un-mission-says-grounds-to-believe-us-committed-war-crimes-in-iran" /><summary type="html">A UN fact-finding mission on Iran said on Thursday it had reasonable grounds to believe the United States was behind two military strikes on a school and sports facility in Iran in February, and that these constituted war crimes. It also found that Iranian authorities committed crimes against humanity during their deadly crackdown on anti-government protests. France 24’s Kethevane Gorjestani takes a closer look at the report’s findings.</summary></entry><entry><title>‘We cried the whole way’: Refugees flee Yemen fighting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8f7f1053d51207a48631ccc4c05a9fa1ee776df89d9c8ae640c199b5603ea499</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T09:24:08Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260918-we-cried-the-whole-way-refugees-flee-yemen-fighting" /><summary type="html">An estimated 125,000 people, including more than 57,000 children, have fled since hostilities erupted in July between the Iran-backed Houthi rebels, the Yemeni government and its ally Saudi Arabia, with the UN calling it one of the most rapid and volatile waves of displacement in Yemen in years. Thousands have even been making the dangerous crossing across the Bab el-Mandeb strait to Djibouti, many of them children, travelling in extreme heat, often without enough water.</summary></entry><entry><title>Russia seizes assets of Swiss food giant Nestle and three French firms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cffd6ea9275dd179591712225c6e7677be68b11eae684e818c0eec22f1581956</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T09:11:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-russia-seizes-assets-of-swiss-food-giant-nestle-and-three-french-firms" /><summary type="html">Russian President Vladimir Putin signed a decree on Thursday to transfer assets of Swiss food giant Nestle and three French groups to a company called LEV Management. Most Western companies quickly sold their Russian operations and holdings after Moscow launched its full-scale invasion of Ukraine, and the Kremlin has since made it difficult for firms to leave the country.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Far-right politician Éric Zemmour joins 2027 French presidential race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a8bedf282d297970bb0252256d1e69e056e685342b7ce5103f882d7c614f8c1</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T09:06:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260918-far-right-politician-%C3%A9ric-zemmour-joins-2027-french-presidential-race" /><summary type="html">French far-right politician Éric Zemmour said on Friday that he would run in next year's presidential election, joining far-right candidate Marine Le Pen, who was runner-up to President Emmanuel Macron in the last two elections. Zemmour is campaigning on a crackdown on immigration, including a plan to expel unemployed foreigners even if they are legal residents.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Fear and broken families: Inside a Texas ICE detention centre</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:102a0584f1f26d93d78f49301c91282843b9be0af9e20b9364abcb3872fab097</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T08:26:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/reporters/20260918-reporters-fear-and-broken-families-inside-a-texas-ice-detention-centre" /><summary type="html">Since Donald Trump’s return to the White House in January 2025, migrant arrests have surged in the United States. More than 610,000 people have passed through detention centres run by Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE), the federal immigration agency in under two years. The pace only continues to accelerate: in August 2026, nearly 51,000 arrests were made in a single month – a record for Trump’s second term. Who are the people being held in these centres? What are their living conditions like? And how is Trump’s mass deportation policy upending the lives of families settled in the United States? In this report, Valérie Defert and Pierrick Laurent investigate the issue in Texas – the heart of the new US immigration detention system.</summary><category term="Reporters" /></entry><entry><title>'Election without meaningful competition': Russia’s results won't measure support for Putin or war</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4223941251e2ba130073e21c846d35ab32f6f96997aa65c3519d9111c83bc5f2</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T08:14:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/election-without-meaningful-competition-russia-s-results-won-t-measure-support-for-putin-or-war" /><summary type="html">Alison Sargent is pleased to welcome Grégoire Roos, Director of the Europe and Russia and Eurasia Programmes at Chatham House. According to Roos, Russia’s parliamentary election is revealing because of what the electoral process can still tell us about the political system Vladimir Putin has constructed. In the absence of any meaningful competition, and anti-war opposition excluded, Roos argues that the most revealing signals may lie elsewhere: in turnout, the timing of voting, the performance of the remaining parties, and the Kremlin’s effort to frame participation itself as evidence of national unity.</summary></entry><entry><title>French PM vows to cut public spending by €54 billion to reduce deficit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:561a9d7f9410f874b2584133044fe6552b4fdb6a69757c245e958e87942090b8</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T07:23:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260918-french-pm-vows-to-cut-public-spending-by-%E2%82%AC54-billion-to-reduce-deficit" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Sébastien Lecornu said on Thursday that France will cut public spending by €54 billion next year to reduce the country's deficit. The announcement comes seven months ahead of the country's presidential election, and the government is wary of a new wave of demonstrations with a jump in global oil prices sparking concerns over the rising cost of living.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>US approves $24.3 billion sale of 48 F-35 warplanes to Saudi Arabia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c87fa08b2ec8eba171da149b8ac92cf3d903076ddece2a895a0a02c2dc7e69e4</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:29:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260918-us-approves-24-3-billion-sale-of-48-f-35-warplanes-to-saudi-arabia" /><summary type="html">The United States on Thursday said it had approved a $24.3 billion sale of 48 F-35 stealth warplanes to Saudi Arabia. Israel has previously voiced concerns about Riyadh buying F-35s, despite a push to normalise relations.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Early voting begins in US midterms that could see Republicans lose control of Congress</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6766d34058f8ee01c086b64a748600eefdcbb1299870eeb75b9a89968001fc03</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T06:15:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260918-early-voting-begins-in-us-midterms-that-could-see-republicans-lose-control-of-congress" /><summary type="html">In-person early voting for the US midterm elections begins Friday, six weeks ahead of the final November 3 vote, which will determine whether Republicans will maintain their majority in the US House and Senate. Some of the main issues American voters are deciding on are how to navigate the cost-of-living crisis, the war in Iran and President Donald Trump’s aggressive immigration enforcement campaign.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Russia votes in parliamentary election as war in Ukraine drags on</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b7d8d05a2a8daaae82001cc17833293fd49a67c2729842bdbe742ed34302f775</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T05:38:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-russia-votes-in-wartime-parliamentary-election-set-to-secure-the-kremlin-power" /><summary type="html">Polls opened in Russia's Far East on Friday as the country began three days of voting for its parliamentary election, the first since Moscow launched its full-scale invasion of Ukraine. The Kremlin's main party, United Russia, is poised to keep its grip on power alongside other parties aligned with President Vladimir Putin, as the only party that criticised the war was removed from the ballot.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Europa League: Marseille suffer heavy defeat at Besiktas</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e85088bb278b61db79f526d222715758834d0f982ab1847518b881628c7c91c4</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T05:04:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260918-europa-league-marseille-suffer-heavy-defeat-at-besiktas" /><summary type="html">Marseille suffered a heavy 4-1 defeat at Besiktas in Turkey in their opening Europa League match. The result was a fourth consecutive defeat for the French side, who must now prepare for Sunday’s Classique against Paris Saint-Germain at the Vélodrome.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Live: Russia strikes four Ukrainian vessels in Black Sea</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f22c84d93acb766b2a93a1a581a95b000f2fe75874af2cc25a8b1a2023739a2</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T03:16:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-live-voting-begins-in-russia-s-parliamentary-elections--3c581f101d42.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-live-voting-begins-in-russia-s-parliamentary-elections" /><summary type="html">Moscow on Friday struck four Ukrainian cargo vessels in the Black ‌Sea, according to Russian state media. The attacks came as polling stations in Russia opened for the country's first parliamentary election since the start of the war in Ukraine. Follow our liveblog for all the latest updates.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says 'major progress' made towards US military base in Poland</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be58efdaf87284ebe9a55639ab0187df6533ba7220228628ff7e8514844867d1</id><updated>2026-09-18T13:01:24Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T01:04:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-trump-says-major-progress-made-toward-us-military-base-in-poland--fed731656a65.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260918-trump-says-major-progress-made-toward-us-military-base-in-poland" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump said that Washington and Warsaw were making "major progress" towards establishing a US military base in Poland, potentially giving the United States a permanent military foothold on NATO's eastern flank even as his administration reviews its broader troop presence in Europe.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
